Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg/Pcd: report a PCD whose size does not match

The carried-over vendor drivers were built against a different PCD database, so
a token number can land on a PCD of another size. PcdDxe asserts on that
mismatch without naming the token, which makes the cause impossible to find.
Print the token and both sizes so it can be matched against this build's
generated PCD database.

Paths in this patch are relative to the root of the uefi-sheng checkout, so it
applies with a plain "git -C up apply" and no extra prefix option.

diff --git a/Mu_Basecore/MdeModulePkg/Universal/PCD/Dxe/Service.c b/Mu_Basecore/MdeModulePkg/Universal/PCD/Dxe/Service.c
index ccd01b7..6800b3b 100644
--- a/Mu_Basecore/MdeModulePkg/Universal/PCD/Dxe/Service.c
+++ b/Mu_Basecore/MdeModulePkg/Universal/PCD/Dxe/Service.c
@@ -414,6 +414,21 @@ GetWorker (
   //
   ASSERT (TokenNumber + 1 < mPcdTotalTokenCount + 1);
 
+  //
+  // Diagnosis for carried-over vendor drivers: report the token whose size does
+  // not match what the caller expects, so it can be named from the generated
+  // PCD database of this build.
+  //
+  if ((GetSize != 0) && (GetSize != DxePcdGetSize (TokenNumber + 1))) {
+    DEBUG ((
+      DEBUG_ERROR,
+      "PCD MISMATCH token %u: caller expects %u bytes, database has %u\n",
+      (UINT32)(TokenNumber + 1),
+      (UINT32)GetSize,
+      (UINT32)DxePcdGetSize (TokenNumber + 1)
+      ));
+  }
+
   ASSERT ((GetSize == DxePcdGetSize (TokenNumber + 1)) || (GetSize == 0));
 
   // EBC compiler is very choosy. It may report warning about comparison
